===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|gelden}}, from {{der|en|non|gelda|t=to geld, castrate}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*galdijaną|t=to castrate}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰel-|t=to cut}}.<ref>{{R:ine:IEW|434}}</ref><ref name = "OED">{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|geld}}</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|non|geldr|t=yielding no milk, dry}}, {{cog|de|galt}}, {{m|de|gelt|t=not giving milk, barren}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐌹𐌻𐌸𐌰|t=sickle}}.<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|geld}}</ref> Compare the archaic {{cog|de|Gelze|t=castrated swine}} and {{m|de|gelzen|t=to castrate}}, {{cog|da|galt|t=castrated boar}} (from {{cog|non|gǫltr|t=boar, hog}}, cognate with {{cog|en|gilt}} and {{m|en|gilde|t=to geld}}. "[[gelding]]" derives from {{cog|non|geldingr}}.<ref name = "OED" />

====Verb====
{{en-verb|+|+|+,gelt}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[castrate]] a [[male]] (usually an [[animal]]).
#* {{RQ:Woolf Jacob's Room|page=16–17|passage="Poor old Topaz," said Mrs Flanders, as he stretched himself out in the sun, and she smiled, thinking how she had had him '''gelded''', and how she did not like red hair in men.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To [[suppress]] or severely [[reduce]] sexual desire or [[libido]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author={{w|Harry E. Wedeck}}|title=Dictionary of Aphrodisiacs|publisher=The Citadel Press|location=New York|page=213|passage=Camphor if smell'd<br>A man will '''geld'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To [[deprive]] of anything [[essential]]; to [[weaken]].

