From {{inh|en|enm|soliciten}}, {{m|enm|solliciten}}, from {{der|en|fro|soliciter}}, {{m|fro|solliciter}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|sollicitō|t=stir, disturb; look after}}, from {{m|la|sollicitus|t=agitated, anxious, punctilious|lit=thoroughly moved}}, from {{m|la|sollus|t=whole, entire}} + perfect passive participle of {{m|la|cieō|t=shake, excite, cite, to put in motion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sə-lĭs'ĭt}}, {{IPA|en|/səˈlɪsɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-solicit.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-solicit.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪsɪt|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[persistent]]ly [[endeavor]] to [[obtain]] an object, or [[bring about]] an event.
