===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:drawen|tree=1}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|dragen}}, {{m|enm|draghen}}, {{m|enm|draue}}, {{m|enm|drauen}}, {{m|enm|drauhen}}, {{m|enm|drawe}}, {{m|enm|drawen}}, {{m|enm|draȝe}}, {{m|enm|draȝen}}, {{m|enm|draȝhenn|t=to drag, pull; to draw (out); to attract; to entice, lure; to lead; to make a drawing; to move, travel; etc.}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=drauen|pos=v|id=MED12537}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|dragan|t=to drag, draw}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*dragan|t=to carry, haul}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*draganą|t=to carry, draw, pull}}; further etymology uncertain, often said to be from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-|t=to drag, pull, run}}, but possibly from a non-Indo-European {{glossary|substrate}} root which is also the source of {{cog|la|trahō|t=to pull, draw; etc.}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=9244711865|date=March 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> {{doublet|en|drag|draught}}.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|drau}}, {{m|enm|draue|t=action of shooting with a bow}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=drau(e|pos=n|id=MED12536}}</ref> from {{m|enm|drauen}}, {{m|enm|drawen|pos=v}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=8574686461|date=March 2025}}</ref>
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|drai}}, {{m|frr|dreeg}}, {{m|frr|dreege|t=to carry; to wear}}, {{cog|fy|drage|t=to carry}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|draan}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|drage}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|droon|t=to bear, carry}}, {{cog|nl|dragen|t=to carry; to wear; to transfer}}, {{cog|de|tragen|t=to bear, carry; to wear; to support}}, {{cog|nds|dregen|t=to carry, take}}, {{cog|lb|droen|t=to carry; to hold, support; to wear; to travel; to fruit}}, {{cog|yi|טראָגן|t=to carry, to wear; to be pregnant}}, {{cog|zea|draege}}, {{m|zea|draoge|t=to carry}}, {{cog|da|drage|t=to draw}}, {{cog|ovd|drågå|t=to drag, draw, pull}}, {{cog|fo,is|draga|t=to drag, draw, pull}}, {{cog|gmq-gut|dräga|t=to pull}}, {{cog|nb|dra}}, {{m|nb|drage|t=to drag, draw, pull}}, {{cog|nn|dra}}, {{m|nn|draga}}, {{m|nn|drage}}, {{m|nn|drågå}}, {{m|nn|dråggå|t=to drag, pull; to leave}}, {{cog|sv|dra}}, {{m|sv|draga|t=to draw, pull; to consume; to leave; to run; to steep}}, {{cog|got|𐌳𐍂𐌰𐌲𐌰𐌽|t=to carry, draw, pull}}; also {{cog|sga|droch|t=wheel; circlet}}, {{cog|la|tragō}}, {{m|la|trahō|t=to drag, pull; to trail; to extract; to plunder; to draw out; to protract; to consider, ponder, weigh}}, {{cog|el|τρέχω|t=to run; to flee; to flow; to execute}}, {{cog|ru|дро́га|t=rail or perch in a cart}}, {{cog|hy|դուրգ|t=to potter’s wheel}}. 
